erations, MGM China, and MGM Digital. The company operates casino resorts that offer gaming, hotel, convention, dining, entertainment, retail, and other resort amenities, as well as online/digital games through its online platforms. Its casino operations include slots and table games, as well as live dealer, online sports betting, and iGaming through BetMGM. The company's customers include premium gaming customers; leisure and wholesale travel customers; business travelers; and group customers, including conventions, trade associations, and small meetings. The company was formerly known as MGM MIRAGE and changed its name to MGM Resorts International in June 2010. MGM Resorts International was incorporated in 1986 and is based in Las Vegas, Nevada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William Joseph Hornbuckle IV | President, CEO & Director | Age 67 | Compensation: $15.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 60K people. Revenue per employee of $292K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $24K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 52\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["MGM Resorts International is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $8.5B market cap on $17.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 9% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $1.5B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 12.29\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 14.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 28% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 60% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6011609399868927},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 54% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $51.7M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Dodge & Cox's Top Q3 2026 Move: Danaher Corp at a 1.17% Portfolio Impact","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/dodge-coxs-top-q3-2026-220421965.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794607461.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Realty Income (O) vs. VICI (VICI): Higher Yield, but Caesars (CZR) Is the Catch","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/real-estate/articles/realty-income-o-vs-vici-121152677.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794571912.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Convicted sex offender gets plea deal in new child sex crime case","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/convicted-sex-offender-gets-plea-000327000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794530129.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.718,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"'Yellowstone' creator Taylor Sheridan on running a historic $330 million ranch","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/yellowstone-creator-taylor-sheridan-running-200650000.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794514422.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"US hotels saw 11% RevPAR uptick in September, highest increase since 2023: CoStar","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/real-estate/arti